                  <msItem>
                     <title>Thomas Rudborne, Chronicon</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">4 quires 18, 28, 36, 48; 49 long lines. It
                        seems likely that this MS., which belonged to Bale, is the one which he saw
                        at All Souls Coll. (Index, p. 452). No other copy of the shorter chronicle
                        (Inc.: 'Multi nobilis ac pietatis studio') is known. The MS. now ends
                        imperfect at 1177, but a note in the Phillipps cat. says that it went to 18
                        H. iiii, 'a quaternio being lost at the end'.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Bale's hand occurs on fol. 176r.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
